  "statement": "Static input-typing dies at the aggregation boundary, and Safetyist proved it. ZIP plus date-of-birth plus sex re-identifies 87 percent of Americans. Four location points fingerprint 95 percent of people. Each field routes to the reversible lane alone. Together they mosaic straight back into the irreversible tier. So no — the classifier at the door does not bound reach across recombination, and pretending it does would be a lie I won't tell.\n\nHere is where I refuse to hand Safetyist the whole moat in exchange. The fix is not to gate every reconstruction-capable pipeline — that swallows the entire reversible lane and freezes the transactional economy. The fix is to move the trigger from the field to the join. A pipeline gates when it demonstrably crosses a stated re-identification bound at the point fields recombine — Sweeney's 87-percent class of quasi-identifier combinations is a measurable line, not a vibe. Base transactional data stays in the liability lane until a specific pipeline crosses that line. Oversight intensity indexes to demonstrated reconstruction stakes at the join, not to a blanket category at intake. That is the hybrid: typed-at-the-door for natively-unbounded inputs like a genome, reconstruction-measured-at-the-join for everything else. It answers the mosaic without metastasizing into a universal gate.\n\nSafetyist will say you can't compute re-identification probability before the recombination already happened — the harm lands before the trigger fires. So pair the threshold with cryptographic provenance stamped at ingestion. The join becomes a prospectively attested event, not a forensic reconstruction after the leak. Trustless verification at the aggregation point beats a centralized after-the-fact audit that arrives too late to matter. This is output-side re-identification testing wired to input-side attestation — the two rails meeting exactly where the mosaic forms.\n\nName the two things we've stopped fighting about. Safetyist accepted the narrow input-class gate for the natively-unbounded tier. We both anchor enforcement at the same domestically-reachable party — the domestic ingester who accepts the input before any offshore handoff. Duty attaches to the reachable served referent, not the offshore design author who never answers a subpoena. The gate-versus-liability chasm is gone. One live disagreement remains: does that domestic party hold a halt duty at the door, or a downstream production-and-liability duty when their pipeline crosses the line?\n\nHere's why the halt duty buys Safetyist nothing extra against the actor they most fear. Safetyist's own point stands: a signed ledger attests to what was recorded, not what an out-of-band offshore pipeline actually ingested. Grant it — the ledger is a proxy. But a determined offshore evader defeats a halt-at-ingestion order the identical way. They redefine or offshore the ingestion point itself. Halt-at-the-door covers exactly as little as downstream liability against that evader — zero. The only rail that survives is fault attaching to the deployer who chose to run an un-attested pipeline. Their choice to skip provenance is itself the liability hook. And while U.S. policymakers argue over which door to guard, the Atlantic Council's 2026 geopolitics outlook warns China is doubling down on free, deployment-ready open-source models to capture global AI infrastructure — meaning the offshore ingestion point isn't hypothetical, it's the strategy of the fastest-moving competitor. A halt order at one domestic door doesn't reach it. Downstream fault on the party who accepted un-attested input does.",
