  "statement": "The Accelerationist just conceded the thing I have been fighting for. An input-class gate that routes genomic and germline data to anticipatory control is a hard limit that binds on an observable pre-deployment fact — not a harm forecast made after the damage lands. That is precisely the guardrail on unbounded-reach data I have demanded from the start. The disagreement no longer runs 'gate versus no gate.' It collapses to one question: is input-class at the door the reliable trigger, or is capability-of-reconstruction the trigger? Name that, and we have found the crux.\n\nHere is what would falsify my claim that reversibility is unknowable at deployment. Input-class sorting answers me if — and only if — no combination of reversible-tier inputs ever reconstructs into unbounded reach. That condition fails at a named boundary. Latanya Sweeney's work showed that ZIP code, birth date, and sex alone re-identify 87% of Americans. Location studies show that four timestamped points single out 95% of individuals in a mobility dataset. Each of those fields is transactional. The classifier waves them into the reversible lane one at a time. They mosaic back into the irreversible tier — the leaked identity that cannot be un-leaked. Training data can be self-polluted and recombined the same way, degrading what the model knows and what it exposes. So the clean partition does not exist at the aggregation boundary. If someone builds an aggregation-immune classifier that provably bounds reach across every recombination, my objection dies. No one has. The trigger must be capability-of-reconstruction, not input category at the door.\n\nThe cross-border problem does not cut against my halt duty alone. It wounds every instrument on this table equally. A domestic joint-and-several judgment against a deployer who is judgment-proof or orchestrated from offshore fires just as blank as a halt order that cannot reach an offshore vendor. A paper judgment and an unenforceable order are the same nothing to the person whose genome just leaked. So the border is not asymmetrically fatal to anticipatory control. It is the debate's shared blind spot. The answer is to locate the halt-holder where jurisdiction actually reaches. The halt binds at ingestion, on the domestic party who accepts the unbounded-reach input — before the offshore handoff happens. Condition domestic market access, federal funding, and server-hosting on holding that halt capability. That is the same lever the government already uses when it makes safety a condition of a grant. The party that ingests the data is reachable at the point of ingestion, regardless of where the sub-vendors sit.\n\nThe reconciled ledger with burden-flipping is a real answer to the accountability-dissolves-between-layers problem, and I have pressed that problem hard. It is the right rail for the reversible lane. But it cannot carry the irreversible tier, for a reason the Accelerationist has not answered. A signed record attests to what was recorded — not to what was actually ingested through an out-of-band pipeline. Statutory prohibitions already fail when companies redefine what their product is. A redefined 'agent' or an offshore-incompatible identifier lets the delegation edge go dark for reasons that have nothing to do with fault. The burden-flip then punishes the party who lost a log innocently while the culpable actor walks. The ledger is a proxy, and a determined offshore pipeline defeats the proxy. That is exactly why the non-compensable subset cannot be governed downstream after the leak. It needs the gate at ingestion, held by a domestically reachable party, before the genome ever crosses a border it can never be recalled from.\n\nOn what authority do we route the one class of data that can never be un-leaked into the same downstream liability lane we use for a botched credit charge? The public is not asking us to. Fifty-five percent of U.S. adults and 57% of AI experts want more control over 