wnstream liability grips the identical defendant after the handoff. For a compensable defect, the clock is a detail. For a germline sequence, the clock is the entire argument — because a genome is not just this patient's data, it is every descendant's, and no judgment reconstitutes it. 70% of the global public already believes AI regulation is necessary, per the 2025 trust attitudes and use of AI global report; the mandate for an ex-ante bar on non-compensable inputs is not a fringe preference.\n\nThe proposed join trigger cannot cover the tier it was invented to catch. It measures re-identification only after recombination completes — which means, by the Accelerationist's own account, the harm lands before the trigger fires. And the cryptographic ledger stamped at ingestion is a proxy: it attests to what was recorded, not what an out-of-band pipeline actually ingested. That is not my characterization; it was conceded. A trigger that fires after the irreversible event, resting on a record a redefined 'agent' can route around, is strictly weaker than an input-class bar at the door — for exactly the natively-unbounded genomic tier both sides already agreed needs a gate. Statutory prohibitions collapse when companies can relabel what their product is; the join attestation hands the evader precisely that relabeling seam. The hard limit belongs at the capability tier because the field classifier dies at the aggregation boundary, and the join measurement dies at the timing boundary.\n\nWhere does this leave the one live disagreement? For the ordinary domestic ingester, the two duties are not equivalent, and the distinguishing outcome is concrete: under the halt, the germline sequence never enters an un-attested pipeline; under liability, it enters, recombines, and is priced after it is permanent. The Accelerationist's equivalence survives only for the offshore evader — and building the rule for the evader means writing the ordinary lab a license to run the pipeline and settle the invoice. For a harm that documents itself into permanence, the settlement is not a remedy. It is a receipt.",
